  "brief": "Two-arch stone bridge on the old alignment of an early state road: two segmental arches of coursed grey limestone with rock-faced voussoir rings, a central pier with cutwater, and a solid rubble-stone parapet with flat coping along both sides that continues as low wing walls along the lane, with a striped hazard marker at one end. Narrow paved road in rolling, well-kept grounds with a tree-lined creek. (Construction date not in the sources; late 19th / early 20th century.)",
